# "Globals touched" ledger -- Firefox 140.12.0esr, probe run. CHECKED-IN EVIDENCE.
#
# This is the raw, unedited output of `vitrin-shim --globals-log`, produced by
# the run described below. It is the evidence the v0 global set is argued
# from: every interface Firefox asks for and does NOT get is refused with a
# written reason in firefox.md, indexed by firefox-refused-globals.txt.
#
# THIS IS A RUN OF THE SHIM AS IT SHIPS, so it is NOT where the argument for
# adding `wl_subcompositor` lives -- that global is in the v0 set by the time
# this run happens, so no probe is armed for it (ledger.c, in_v0_contract) and
# it can only appear here as `class=v0` offers and binds. A successful bind is
# the weaker signal; the demand line is the stronger one, and it is in the
# pre-addition run checked in beside this file as
# globals-demand-wl_subcompositor-140.12.0esr.log. An earlier version of this
# header claimed the demand line was in THIS file. It never was.
#
# HOW TO REGENERATE (verbatim; the only variable is the temp dir):
#
#   bash shim/tests/firefox/fetch-esr.sh
#   meson compile -C shim/build
#   RT=$(mktemp -d); chmod 700 "$RT"
#   export XDG_RUNTIME_DIR="$RT" WLR_BACKENDS=headless WLR_RENDERER=pixman \
#          WLR_RENDERER_ALLOW_SOFTWARE=1 WLR_LIBINPUT_NO_DEVICES=1
#   unset WAYLAND_DISPLAY DISPLAY
#   ./shim/build/mock-core --size 1024x768 --run-ms 22000 \
#     -- ./shim/build/vitrin-shim --socket ff0 --probe-globals \
#        --globals-log "$RT/g.log" >"$RT/core.log" 2>"$RT/shim.log" &
#   # ... wait for $RT/ff0, then, with a fresh profile carrying
#   # shim/tests/firefox/profile.user.js as user.js:
#   env -i HOME="$RT/prof" XDG_RUNTIME_DIR="$RT" WAYLAND_DISPLAY=ff0 \
#       PATH=/usr/bin:/bin MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1 GDK_BACKEND=wayland \
#       MOZ_ACCELERATED=0 LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1 MOZ_CRASHREPORTER_DISABLE=1 \
#       GTK_A11Y=none NO_AT_BRIDGE=1 \
#       timeout 22 shim/.firefox/firefox/firefox --profile "$RT/prof" \
#       --no-remote "file://$PWD/shim/tests/firefox/pages/repaint.html"
#
# WHAT TO READ FIRST:
#   `globals-demand:`  -- the crux. Each one is Firefox binding an interface
#                         the v0 set does not provide. These are only visible
#                         because --probe-globals advertised them; without it
#                         a wanted-but-absent interface produces NO WIRE
#                         TRAFFIC AT ALL (see shim/include/ledger.h).
#   `globals-touched:` -- one aggregate row per interface, at the end.
#   `globals-summary:` -- totals. `drift=0` means the advertised v0 set and
#                         the contract list in ledger.c agree.
#
# CONTEXT FOR THIS RUN:
#   Firefox   140.12.0esr (pinned, sha256-verified; tests/firefox/firefox-esr.pin)
#   shim      p1.6.4-firefox-bringup, --probe-globals, 20 probes armed
#             (21 in the catalogue; wl_subcompositor is excluded because it
#             is now a real global, so probing it would shadow the real one)
#   renderer  headless wlroots + pixman, software WebRender, no GPU
#   clients   3 connections -- Firefox's parent process makes two (a short
#             early one and the long-lived one) and a child process makes one.
#             Their binds are interleaved below; the aggregate rows are what
#             the contract is argued from.
#   result    55 frames forwarded to the core, window mapped, no wire
#             violations, drift=0
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
